Samurai Shodown RPG (Shinsetsu Samurai Spirits: Bushidou Retsuden) — English translation

Unofficial English translation of 真説サムライスピリッツ 武士道烈伝 (PlayStation, SLPS-00814, Japan, SNK 1997).

Patch version: v1.0 · Date: 2026-11-25

This patch is applied to the ORIGINAL JAPANESE game. It does not need, and does not work on, the Spanish translation.
Before and after

In game

What's included

The whole script: prologues of the eight heroes, both stories (Weeping Flower and Evil Heaven), each character's short stories, endings and the special "This is the shop" program.
Menus, battle, techniques, items, equipment, shops, place and enemy names.
System and memory card messages.
Redrawn graphic text: title logo ("SAMURAI SHODOWN — The true legend of Bushido"), character and story selection, shop signs, battle buttons and gauges, "One moment..." and the "Cut!" brush caption.
Distinct character voices: American English for most of the cast, British English for Ukyo, Charlotte's French, Cham Cham and Tam Tam's pidgin, Galford's CAPS, Earthquake's "GF", Gen-an's "ke"…
What you need

Your own copy of the game. It is not included.
Check that your image matches the Redump dump:
File	SHA-1	CRC32
Shinsetsu Samurai Spirits - Bushidou Retsuden (Japan) (Track 1).bin	7f1f66f75189e1be3e5909330a7d0a4a2863f9e6	207309bc
Shinsetsu Samurai Spirits - Bushidou Retsuden (Japan) (Track 2).bin	bdf431028e61f3edd9b507bb6756c1c0f87ae95f	7023155b
Shinsetsu Samurai Spirits - Bushidou Retsuden (Japan) (Track 3).bin	3b60e5eaaedb0e2e0247be85244782b8be597cf4	a1fd605a
Shinsetsu Samurai Spirits - Bushidou Retsuden (Japan) (Track 4).bin	b3cc95636253c271ee55dcabeff8d6ea50cd84b8	b8b1eebd
The patch only changes track 1 (data). Audio tracks are copied as they are.
If your copy is a single .bin with every track, that's fine: the patcher detects it.
Installation

Windows

Download and unzip the latest file from Releases.
Copy your game's .cue and .bin files into the parche folder.
Double-click Apply_on_Windows.bat (needs Python 3).
… (EN).bin and … (EN).cue will be created in the same folder.
Manual alternative: open Delta Patcher, choose your (Track 1).bin, the .bps file and click Apply patch. Keep the original (Track 2–4).bin files next to the .cue.

macOS

Download and unzip the latest file from Releases.
Copy your game's .cue and .bin files into the parche folder.
Double-click Apply_on_Mac.command.
If macOS blocks it: right-click → Open → Open.
If you don't have Python 3, the script tells you how to install it.
… (EN).bin and … (EN).cue will be created.
Terminal alternative (macOS):

python3 apply_translation.py "/full/path/to/Shinsetsu Samurai Spirits - Bushidou Retsuden (Japan).cue"
Linux

python3 apply_translation.py "/full/path/to/Shinsetsu Samurai Spirits - Bushidou Retsuden (Japan).cue"
Expected result (translated data track): SHA-1 6ac284e3c3551762bb2cc76ac9152633db39b8ea, CRC32 b8f8b61c. The patcher checks it automatically.

How to play

Tested on RetroArch with PCSX ReARMed (BIOS SCPH-5500). Load the (EN).cue file. Enable the memory card so you can save.

Translation decisions

Item	Decision	Reason
Title logo	"SAMURAI SHODOWN — The true legend of Bushido", redrawn	The series' Western name
Character names	Official Western names of the series (Haohmaru, Nakoruru, Galford, Ukyo, Genjuro, Cham Cham…)	Project preference
Ukyo's dialogue	British English	He is extremely polite and refined
Charlotte's French words	Kept	Part of her identity
Techniques with Japanese names	Romanized ("Kogetsuzan", "Tenha Danku Retsuzan")	As in the Western releases
Battle buttons	ATK · TEC · RUN · SCT · ITM · DEF · ANN · FRM	Each box fits 3 letters
Rage gauge	IRE	"RAGE" does not fit in 13 pixels
Item names in shop lists	Abbreviated to 12 letters ("Pnts.", "Sndls.", "Brclt.")	List width
Intro card, title menu, ADJUST SCREEN	Kept	Already in English
Opening video (calligraphy 斬れ / 死…)	Kept in Japanese	Text burned into the video
End credits	Kept	Already in English
SNK・フジテレビ・ASATSU	Kept	Company credits
Save title in the memory card manager	Kept in Japanese	Shown by the console BIOS
Full glossary: docs/glossary_v1.0.csv · Character voices: docs/style_guide.md · Decisions: docs/translation_decisions.md

The English text was translated mainly from the finished Spanish translation by the same author, checking the Japanese original whenever needed.

Known issues

The opening video keeps its Japanese captions.
Save files made with other versions of the game may show the place name in another language on the save screen until you save again.
This is a first release: the game is very long and could not be played through entirely. If you find untranslated or cut-off text or a typo, please report it (see below).
How to report a bug

Open an issue with the "Report a bug" template (docs/report_bug.md) and include:

Patch version and emulator/console, with version and core.
Where it happens: story, character, screen, what you were doing.
What you expected and what you saw: cut-off text, untranslated text, typo, crash, etc.
A screenshot and, if possible, a save or RetroArch state just before the problem.
For crashes: does it also happen with the original game?
Typos and style suggestions are welcome too.

